  "note": "Full supplied measured point clouds, no thinning, one production analysis worker and pool. Five warm-up pairs precede alternating sequential scalar/SIMD comparisons for each workflow. Standalone voxel scores rebuild both Gaussian maps and calculate fresh AWD/SCS. Combined Map quality uses warm retained nearest preparation, scalar exact f64 searches, queued dispatch, progressive joins, adaptive summaries and original f32 inlier arithmetic. No Gaussian maps, distance arrays or voxel scores are cached. Only independent voxel moment channels change: SIMD performs two f64 components per instruction, with the same per-channel point order and separate multiply/add operations; voxel keys, occupancy, covariance conversion, Wasserstein eigensolvers and SCS arithmetic stay the same. Wall times include fresh computation and RPCs, plus searches, joins, summaries and metrics for combined Map quality. Loading, pool startup/warming, validation and exports are excluded; combined worker millis are recorded separately. Every comparison preserves voxel counts and allows only existing 1e-12 relative/absolute HashMap reduction roundoff in AWD/SCS. Combined comparisons also require all displayed distance bits, f64 statistics and inlier metrics to match exactly, with identical lane counts and retained input bytes. Source/manifest and artifact hashes are recorded. Other applications, CPU clocks, power and GC are uncontrolled. Measured-source even/odd subsets are not independent surveys or accuracy ground truth."
